{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced","id":1523460,"title":"Anyone else feel that at a certain resource level VTM becomes forced?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-02T06:27:32-07:00","id":1523460,"title":"Anyone else feel that at a certain resource level VTM becomes forced?","content":"It may just be me, but at resource 4 and 5, maybe 3 if you really push it, a lot of the threats to your charachter can easily be avoided. When you have enough money for a private security team and a plane in and out of a city at anytime, it feels kind of forced.<br /> <br /> That just me though. What about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T06:38:36-07:00","id":1523461,"title":"","content":"When you have that kind of resources you start to look as a pawn for bigger players like methusaleah while also having to deal with people who want to take those resources for them.<br /> <br /> Chances are that such big resources are controlled through some kind of organization or intermediary, ex the ballard group. Vampires have access to blood bond, dominate and pressence to wrestle those assets from you.<br /> <br /> Also in certain circunstances you might not have access to them. Not to mention that the security team might not work against an Assamite sent against you, a blood hunt, an angry prince and his mobs etc... or the fact that you have to reach the airport.<br /> <br /> Resources 5 is stronger than disciplines at equal level, but that does not mean you are invincible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T06:45:41-07:00","id":1523462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523461#post1523461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have that kind of resources you start to look as a pawn for bigger players like methusaleah while also having to deal with people who want to take those resources for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Oh of course, I'm just trying to say that a lot of the lower level threats such as Hunters and a Sabbat siege feel forced when you have a ton of money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 10-02-2023, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T06:58:41-07:00","id":1523463,"title":"","content":"Having those resources brings more headache than you think!<br /> Money is noticable, trackable, and makes you a target - depending of the source of course could even have dangerous consequences (unwanted attention from other forces like Wraith, Lupin/Garou, Changeling, Mage, etc...)<br /> A Sabbat siege is more painfull for those who have something to loss<br /> Similarly, Hunters could follow the money and track back to you - well competent Hunters<br /> Not to mention, most lower level characters have 0 idea and experience how to be rich and influental and it blows up in their face <br /> Anything abowe 3 is a treasuretrove of conflict in the hands of GM<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T07:45:57-07:00","id":1523465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced#post1523460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may just be me, but at resource 4 and 5, maybe 3 if you really push it, a lot of the threats to your charachter can easily be avoided. When you have enough money for a private security team and a plane in and out of a city at anytime, it feels kind of forced.<br /> <br /> That just me though. What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look... this is a stereotypical view, using money is not something simple, when it comes to paying someone to do such a thing, this thought makes you very susceptible to being a victim of scams, but that's not the point. Even if you have 5 points in resources, unless you plan to be isolated in a building like a fort, you will still be vulnerable, you can take a team of security guards, but inside the city they will not be of much help as you cannot You'll think of using a bazooka or a machine gun in the middle of the street and hoping that the mask doesn't fall off or that it doesn't attract attention, especially if the game takes place in 2015 and beyond.<br /> <br /> Also, there are people who cannot be bought, or who are more susceptible to fear, and vampiric power you the thing. One idea I had to illustrate this kind of thing was that your character needs an informant from the underworld or something like that, he can roll the dice using resources as a bonus (Charisma + Streetwise + Resources) something like that.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, there's a funny situation I saw once, a group was trapped in a cave-in underneath a cemetery (I don't remember what they were doing) and one of them who had resources 3 or 4 wanted to order a jackhammer to get them out, the ST asked them to check with contacts to see if anyone knew anyone capable of getting the material, the player was &quot;stressed&quot; because he was rich, but it was 3:30 in the morning and there was no service open at that time, money would'n help so much in this situation.<br /> <br /> But yeah, with a good preparation money can avoid much headache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T09:45:22-07:00","id":1523468,"title":"","content":"Resources in VtM is both very powerful and useless at the same time, with the deciding factor being how well both the Players and the ST understand how money actually works, rather than just copying what they have seen in movies or on social media. Resources functions a lot like poker chips in that even if you don't have the cards to win the hand, you can still either buy the pot or bluff by using your chips as psychological leverage. Alternatively, you could just consider Money to be Blue cards in a Magic the Gathering game.<br /> <br /> But here is a big catch, the instant you go across a boarder, your Resources level changes with the exchange rate and access to banks. A person can live quite comfortably in say Thailand on about $1,000 a month. Over there that is Resources 3-4, but in the US making $10,000 a year is considered poverty level to the point that you barely pay any taxes, so it would abstractly round out to about Resources 0-1. <br /> <br /> I think the real problem is that most people don't think about how their characters money works. When I play a high Resources character, I tend to flush out a lot of financial backstories and contingency plans. Meaning that if you have Resources 5, you own multiple businesses, each of which has its own perks, you own multiple havens, you have caches setup to deal with emergencies, you have isolated revenue streams so that if any one business gets targeted it won't affect the rest of your infrastructure. Now when you put that kind of thought into Resources, it is OP as hell, but if you are in the middle of wilderness with Lupines chasing you, a roll of hundreds is only good for tinder.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair there was one game where the PC coterie used Resources to leverage a cease fire of sorts with some local shifters. They bought the bank which had the debts of all the local kinfolk and their mortgages. In exchange for forgiving the debts and pouring money into the community, the vampires were allowed to coexist in the area as long as they behaved. It also helped that if the vampires got killed off, legal clauses would mean the entire area would be rezoned and bulldozed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T10:00:45-07:00","id":1523469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced#post1523460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may just be me, but at resource 4 and 5, maybe 3 if you really push it, a lot of the threats to your charachter can easily be avoided.<br /> When you have enough money for a private security team and a plane in and out of a city at anytime, it feels kind of forced.<br /> That just me though. What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never found it a issue as high resources can help with many problems, but it won't get rid of them entirely and as some of the above posters mentioned that money leaves a trail that smart operators can track and especially in a post 9/11 world where taking out of certain amount of money raises red flags for law enforcement and the banking industry and not to mention what do you mean by resources? You can have lots of assets but can only get a limited amount made available on short notice as it could be tied up in investments or through third parties to give you certain protection and you might not have time to get in touch with them.<br /> <br /> Also as mentioned is how did they get this money in the first place? I sometimes try to work out why say my Malkavian outside from coming from a well off family has been able to maintain it or think outside of the box of saying maybe I have a Ministry member who crashes at a wealthy backer's home through good use of Presence &amp; blood bonding and uses said person's skill to spread his or her message of Set. But is ready to get out of dodge if things get heated.<br /> <br /> In short there is many ways that high level resources can not handle all problems with great ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-12-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T12:26:58-07:00","id":1523471,"title":"","content":"One of the big reasons I adapted the Availability and related rules from the CofD for WoD games, is because as noted, most people have no idea how money works once the numbers get too big. Those rules might not be some amazing attempt at realism, but they're good enough and more important they communicate much more clearly what money can accomplish in the game; including what happens when money, and other forms of power and influence, start to butt heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T14:22:09-07:00","id":1523473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523463#post1523463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having those resources brings more headache than you think!\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I think STs have problems with high Resources when they are not being creative enough. Or perhaps more fairly, I should say people are unfamiliar enough with finance to know what its limitations are. People have a tendency to think fairly one dimensionally. If a person surrounds himself with bodyguards, then it means I cannot run a plot to attempt to kill the character via X so that means I cannot run any plot. But instead that should just mean the antagonists have to address the issue from another angle. STs and Players often want to run &quot;street level&quot; style games, and in these cases having a Resources 5 PC can eliminate that style of play. But all that means is that the PC is not appropriate for the chronicle, not that there is nothing the ST can do to challenge the player. It's just that the style of game that is good for that kind of PC is often unattractive to all the other PCs, and it becomes hard to run the game. In these cases, the gaming group needs to have an OOC discussion on how best to handle this so everyone is having fun.<br /> <br /> And as you say, having lots of money means you are more noticeable and potentially might attract other enemies, or provide another opportunity for your enemies to hurt you in another way.<br /> <br /> I know current rules sets are much more nebulous, but originally Resources 5 may have made you a millionaire in net worth, but the actual extra cash to do something per month was something like $30k. in the nineties. That's still only around $40k nowadays. That's enough money to help your character grease some palms, buy a used car in cash to use as a getaway vehicle for the coterie, hire a lawyer to get a coterie mate out of jail, and other things. It is not something that allows you to ignore the world.<br /> <br /> At an extra $40k a month, that's not quite half a million dollars you have for the entire year if you spend it on personal protection. But all it does it get you into the world of Hollywood Celebrity bodyguard protection. It keeps out the riffraff, paparazzi, and stalkers from getting too close to you. It's not the kind of protection that allows you to prevent Assamites killing you or withstand a Sabbat siege. To simulate that level of protection, it's about the same as a Retainer and some Allies. And by having that kind of protection, you pretty much eliminate all the free cash that Resources provides.<br /> <br /> Resources 5 was never about Bruce Wayne and Tony Stark level wealth. It was that of a successful local businessman who now has passive wealth. Of course, if your ST allows you can have access to 6+ Backgrounds that will increase that and eventually get to those levels. But all that means is the nature of the game changes at that point.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T18:51:15-07:00","id":1523482,"title":"","content":"My richest character was a Malkavian. She was a stock market investor that broke her fortune in several currencies and sent all around the globe. She was a blast to interpret, because she acted as the stereotype a Ventrue would have of a Malkavian while she hacked and sent the prince's fortune here and there. And who would suspect of the lady cosplaying as the Mad Hatter talking to the bush?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T03:46:39-07:00","id":1523490,"title":"","content":"The thing about private security teams is, unless you're prepared to Dominate and/or Blood Bond them, they ironically represent a security risk as far as the Masquerade is concerned.<br /> <br /> They know your comings and goings. If you take them out on the town, do you just send them away while you're feeding? What if they accidently see? Disciplines, pay-offs, and Ghouling can mitigate the immediate threat of your bodyguards finding out you're a vampire. But they still know, and that means they could be compromised, one way or another. The more private security you have Ghouled, the bigger the drain on your own Vitae every month. You need to keep track of them all, and not neglect any of them. Ghouls are also...volatile, let's say, due to the influence of the Vitae in their system and their addiction.<br /> <br /> Obviously, older vampires deal with this as a matter of course. The benefits of having tons of Ghouled security outweigh the costs for them. But those ARE still issues, that younger Kindred (or other parties) can exploit.<br /> <br /> On another note, moving around with a team of bodyguards draws attention. If you've got a stable Herd or have other means of bringing vessels to you, great. But if not, everyone is going to know when the local rich VIP who only ever comes out at night is on the town. They'll remember if they go necking some customer at a nightclub, especially if they end up dead accidently. A Kindred's ability to be anonymous goes down proportional to the number of dudes in suits and ear-pieces follow them around.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind those bodyguards must also be minimally outfitted, unless you're going on a raid of some kind. You can't take your boys into a nightclub strapped with full military gear. (Unless you're in one of those states with open carry of assault weapons. In which case that advantage goes both ways. Be prepared for your enemies to walk around similarly armed). Point is, if your bodyguards only have concealed handguns, their utility isn't as good as it could be.<br /> <br /> A Haven with strong private security, unless it's out in the woods, is basically impossible to hide. Everyone will know a rich VIP lives there. It might make hunters think twice about attacking it, but it also means they know where you'll be, and can follow you elsewhere. You can't take an entire household's worth of mercenaries with you every time you want to go on adventures. And you couldn't leave your Haven undefended even if you could. Only part of your security detail goes with you, which means the full measure of your Resources doesn't translate to protection when you need to leave your house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T07:19:47-07:00","id":1523494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523490#post1523490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about private security teams is, unless you're prepared to Dominate and/or Blood Bond them, they ironically represent a security risk as far as the Masquerade is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>A security team is less of a risk for the Masquerade than a Herd is, if for no other reason than that they are professionals rather than junkies, homeless people, or college dropouts. Rather than ghouling the entire team, you would be better served to ghoul the team leader. That way the squad is on the perimeter while the leader is the one in charge and staying close enough to you to see anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523490#post1523490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind those bodyguards must also be minimally outfitted, unless you're going on a raid of some kind. You can't take your boys into a nightclub strapped with full military gear. (Unless you're in one of those states with open carry of assault weapons. In which case that advantage goes both ways. Be prepared for your enemies to walk around similarly armed). Point is, if your bodyguards only have concealed handguns, their utility isn't as good as it could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> In the scenario where you drive up to the club in two unmarked black SUVs, you enter through a back entrance rather than the front door to avoid attention. Half the team goes inside, while the other half is on perimeter security outside the club. The vehicles are armored and have the bigger weapons stored inside. Yes the security guards have to blend in, but that is still doable with Type II body armor under a suit that is tailored to hide the armor and weapons rig. Though to be honest, it would be less hassle to just buy the Club rather than trying to sneak your security detail past a third party owner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523490#post1523490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Haven with strong private security, unless it's out in the woods, is basically impossible to hide. Everyone will know a rich VIP lives there. It might make hunters think twice about attacking it, but it also means they know where you'll be, and can follow you elsewhere. You can't take an entire household's worth of mercenaries with you every time you want to go on adventures. And you couldn't leave your Haven undefended even if you could. Only part of your security detail goes with you, which means the full measure of your Resources doesn't translate to protection when you need to leave your house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again it really depends on how the haven is setup and how the PC behaves.<br /> <br /> One example is an office building is the business district of a city. Everyone expects there to be security on the premises, but few people expect an entire floor to be dedicated to being havens for an entire coterie. No one would think twice about a very secure parking garage structure that has a secret entrance to a basement level, etc.<br /> <br /> In one game I had the local Tremere setup a dummy chantry one street over from the real one. They were connected by an underground tunnel, so if anyone was watching the dummy chantry, you would see the Tremere coming and going. But they really resided in a different building with heavy warding, loyalist gargoyles, and plenty of security in the above ground section that was a Bank owned by the coterie. In that game the dummy chantry was more or less a death trap and was &quot;destroyed&quot; many times at great cost to the &quot;victorious&quot; enemies. The Tremere always seemed to come back in the end though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T11:45:31-07:00","id":1523506,"title":"","content":"I would also add a thing like Murphy's Law in such cases as every well crafted plan can go wrong when it hits reality and the older Kindred would know this and would try be flexiable to get to safety or fight. As mentioned that you can't have a large army at your beck and call and most bodyguards job is not get into meaningless battles when there principal is still in danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T14:14:49-07:00","id":1523664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523462#post1523462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Oh of course, I'm just trying to say that a lot of the lower level threats such as Hunters and a Sabbat siege feel forced when you have a ton of money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Smart Hunters would find ways to counter a Kindred resources in a multi-prong attack and in regards to the Sabbat most of the leaders are not that type of stupid and will try to be subtle in a siege by making attacks look like something else and most security ghouls would be cannon fodder as they wouldn't be able to truly match a Ancilla or young Elder in a direct battle unless their lucky that their dominator is a member of the 5th or 6th generation and were able to get them up 3-4 dots in the Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T17:27:49-07:00","id":1523845,"title":"","content":"Sabbat sieges also don't neglect attacks on finances. Whether that's by physically attacking brokers or the businesses that belong to Camarilla Kindred, or by engaging their own &quot;business warriors&quot; (like members of the Order of St Blaise) to engage in hostile takeovers, or simply by throwing so much at Camarilla territories that it taxes the liquidity of the defenders.<br /> <br /> Sure, having Resources 5+ can make some problems go away. But if you need to <i>keep doing that</i>, eventually you'll run out of cash and start having to cannibalize your assets just to keep up the defense. That's why it's a <i>siege</i>.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, for all its faults, has no shortage of shovelheads they can throw at a problem. They can always make more. And if anything, those disappearances that start piling up only really act as a thorn in the side of resident Camarilla vampires. The Sabbat doesn't care, it's not their territory (<b>yet</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T04:37:38-07:00","id":1523870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523845#post1523845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, having Resources 5+ can make some problems go away. But if you need to <i>keep doing that</i>, eventually you'll run out of cash and start having to cannibalize your assets just to keep up the defense. That's why it's a <i>siege</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you can't run out of cash in that fashion. RAW for Resources is that your score only goes down if you make a purchase that is equal to your current score or you have to make several purchases at a level below that, but two or more levels below that are functionally endless. So a Resources 8 Coterie can makes endless Resources 5 or 6 purchases. <br /> <br /> That would mean, to cause financial loss in a meaningful way the attacker, be they Hunter group or Sabbat, would need to inflict Resources 5 or higher in each attack just to have a chance at putting a dent in the targets portfolio. That would be the equivalent of taking down the World Trader Center with every attack and that wouldn't really affect a coterie with a Pooled Resource rating of 8 because of the fact that their interests are so diversified that you would need a coordinated attack that spans states if not countries to achieve that level of damage.<br /> <br /> If the target makes 10 billion dollars a month from dozens of businesses scattered across the globe, doing a bank hack to freeze a couple of accounts and fire bombing a few buildings still doesn't even put a dent in the interest accrued let alone the operating budget. In the case of mortal hunters, they will die of old age before being able to do that much damage.<br /> <br /> But lets say that somehow the stars aligned and by combination of stupidity of the Target, vast amounts of insider knowledge by the attackers, and ST created contrivance to make it possible.... the attackers were able to do enough damage to start lowering the Pooled Resources rating. The Masquerade as a whole would be threatened by this level of attack. This would be the equivalent of multiple WTC attacks every month, the mortal attention alone would bury a hunter and that kind of behavior even the Sabbat wouldn't condone the collateral damage. Other vampires would destroy the attacker just to preserve the masquerade if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T14:32:40-07:00","id":1523886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523870#post1523870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW for Resources is that your score only goes down if you make a purchase that is equal to your current score or you have to make several purchases at a level below that, but two or more levels below that are functionally endless. So a Resources 8 Coterie can makes endless Resources 5 or 6 purchases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I think you might be confusing different iterations of the system. RAW Resources, like all backgrounds, in the WoD system goes up and down as ST discretion based on what's happening in the story. You're describing things like how Exalted and the CofD have tried to implement Resources.<br /> <br /> Also, the RAW for Poled Backgrounds in V20 is that Pooled Resources 6+ is not the same as individual Resources 6+ as detailed in other books. The book points out that a bunch of Resources 1 and 2 characters that pool to 6 aren't supposed to suddenly become billionaires, but rather that high rating represents the resilience their group efforts cause in ensuring their cash flow remains constant; that is, the coterie can endure hard financial times for longer because of their cooperation where as individuals they'd have gone broke.<br /> <br /> Pooled Resources is more like how a well funded and organized union strike fund that allows a union to exercise power against the much more wealthy corporation(s) the union's workers are employed by. During a time where the union members should all be losing personal Resources because they're not getting paid, the strike fund steps in to fill the gaps starting with the most vulnerable members. The more potent the strike fund (aka having large Pooled Resources) the harder it is for the employer(s) to try to wait out a union in the hopes of forcing workers back as their finances dry up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T17:14:17-07:00","id":1523892,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523490#post1523490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about private security teams is, unless you're prepared to Dominate and/or Blood Bond them, they ironically represent a security risk as far as the Masquerade is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why my main character presents as a rich eccentric who hopped on the bandwagon of exotic pets. Ever hear of Siegfried and Roy having their home invaded?\u200b I'll admit, not terribly useful for the character when going out and about, but hunters or rivals' goons breaking in to find where he sleeps during the day soon discover they have more pressing concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T05:17:02-07:00","id":1523911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523886#post1523886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, I think you might be confusing different iterations of the system. RAW Resources, like all backgrounds, in the WoD system goes up and down as ST discretion based on what's happening in the story. You're describing things like how Exalted and the CofD have tried to implement Resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem comes from the extrapolation affect of not doing actual book keeping. So if we look at the rank 4 description of Resources in the V20 book it reads:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wealthy. You rarely touch cash, as most of your assets exist in tangible forms that are themselves more valuable and stable than paper money. You hold more wealth than many of your local peers (if they can be called such a thing). <i><u><b>When earning your Resources doesn\u2019t enjoy your usual degree of attention, you can maintain a three-dot existence for up to a year, <i><b>and a two dot existence indefinitely.</b></i>\u200b</b></u></i> </div> </div> </div>I don't claim that Backgrounds don't go up or down due to ST adjudication or by the ramification of player choices, I am just pointing out that by both the simplified rules of Resources and by the reality of mass earning potential, that once you get into a certain level of profit, you can basically out spend the damage a potential enemy can cause without affecting the profit infrastructure as a whole.<br /> <br /> The description also implies that this is a passive side effect, meaning when all your businesses are on auto-pilot without you, the Background functions as limited one dot lower, and infinite two dots lower. But if you were taking an active control of them, like if you were under financial siege, then that restriction wouldn't apply as you would be taking active counter measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T05:40:15-07:00","id":1523912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523886#post1523886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the RAW for Poled Backgrounds in V20 is that Pooled Resources 6+ is not the same as individual Resources 6+ as detailed in other books. The book points out that a bunch of Resources 1 and 2 characters that pool to 6 aren't supposed to suddenly become billionaires, but rather that high rating represents the resilience their group efforts cause in ensuring their cash flow remains constant; that is, the coterie can endure hard financial times for longer because of their cooperation where as individuals they'd have gone broke.<br /> <br /> Pooled Resources is more like how a well funded and organized union strike fund that allows a union to exercise power against the much more wealthy corporation(s) the union's workers are employed by. During a time where the union members should all be losing personal Resources because they're not getting paid, the strike fund steps in to fill the gaps starting with the most vulnerable members. The more potent the strike fund (aka having large Pooled Resources) the harder it is for the employer(s) to try to wait out a union in the hopes of forcing workers back as their finances dry up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the Pooled Background system specifically mentions the ST considering scaling, but that means in both directions.<br /> <br /> So yes a coterie of five who individually have Resources 2 and each donate one dot to a pooled Resource Background technically have Resources 5 is what that rule section is referring to that they are not all billionaires.<br /> <br /> But then all this gets turned on its head when every member of the Coterie has Resources 5 (Billionaires) individually to start with and then pool the Resources which would mean Resources 25 give or take a dot. Thus the overall potential far exceeds the normal limits rather than the ST down scaling it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, when discussing Resources, especially of this scale, it means there aren't singular things to target. There won't be a single bank account that this all funnels into, hell there won't be a single bank that all of this funnels into. It would be dozens of accounts, spread across many banks, in many countries that store the &quot;liquid&quot; wealth.<br /> <br /> But even if you managed to hack every single bank and drain the accounts, all the infrastructure businesses that produce the income will keep chugging along and produce more wealth and replenish the new accounts. Hence why I say there is a threshold of damage you have to do in a short amount of time otherwise it is meaningless.<br /> <br /> Lastly it is worth pointing out that not every kindred will leave all their wealth in bank accounts. It would be part of their survival strategy to bleed off a percentage of profit every month or year or so and setup contingencies. For example with this level of wealth, you are expected to own multiple Havens. But what if every haven had a hidden stash of gold bars, jewels, etc. so that regardless of what happens to their main Resources, they are right back to at least Resources 5 the instant they walk in the door. Think John Wicks basement stash in the first movie, but on a grander scale, and then he owns houses in every state or major country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T12:54:05-07:00","id":1523922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523911#post1523911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem comes from the extrapolation affect of not doing actual book keeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your original phrasing was not about &quot;extrapolating&quot; from the ability to continue a given quality of life while neglecting your primary income streams. You talked about &quot;Resources X&quot; purchases, which aren't a thing in this variation of the game.<br /> <br /> You clearly have the book handy. Why are you doubling down instead of just acknowledging the mix up and moving on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if we look at the rank 4 description of Resources in the V20 book it reads: </div> </div> </div>Notice how the phrase, &quot;if you make a purchase that is equal to your current score&quot; or something equivalent is nowhere to be found? You just cited that you weren't actually talking about the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't claim that Backgrounds don't go up or down due to ST adjudication or by the ramification of player choices,... </div> </div> </div>You said:<br /> <br /> &quot;RAW for Resources is that your score only goes down if...&quot; and did not include ST adjudication or the ramification of player choices besides making purchases. You might not have intended to make this claim, but you most certainly did phrase it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am just pointing out that by both the simplified rules of Resources... </div> </div> </div>Claiming you're citing the RAW doesn't really cover, citing an optional &quot;simplified&quot; version of the rules that's not even in the core book (or any book? I don't know which simplified version you're talking about, but definitely isn't in V20 core).<br /> <br /> The problem isn't the reality of high end finances. The problem is you vastly overstating what the books say these numbers represent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...you can basically out spend the damage a potential enemy can cause without affecting the profit infrastructure as a whole. </div> </div> </div>Multi-billion dollar companies have collapsed without taking the economy down with them. It's not good for the economy of course, but you're treating trying to bankrupt someone like David Geffen as if you were trying to completely shutdown the entirely of Amazon's complete corporate portfolio (both in terms of difficulty and scale of economic impact).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you were taking an active control of them, like if you were under financial siege, then that restriction wouldn't apply as you would be taking active counter measures. </div> </div> </div>An active enemy vampire siege would be drawing you away from actively running your profitable activity. You can't &quot;day&quot; trade in the Asian markets from the US to maximize the profits of your coterie's activities and stop the Sabbat from burning down your local physical assets at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523912#post1523912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then all this gets turned on its head when every member of the Coterie has Resources 5 (Billionaires) individually to start with and then pool the Resources which would mean Resources 25 give or take a dot. Thus the overall potential far exceeds the normal limits rather than the ST down scaling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the book tells STs to cap Pooled Backgrounds at 10. You'll never have to deal with a coterie throwing around Resources 25 unless you decide to subject yourself to trying to figure out what the hell that means.<br /> <br /> Second, for someone that's been going on (generally quite correctly) about how money really works at these levels, the kind of people that have accumulated and maintained the wealth represented by Resources 5 are not going to put all of their personal assets into a group setup that will level them broke if it collapses (which is what you just suggested they'd do). Hell, just five PCs with Resources 5 dropping themselves to Resources 3 so the coterie would have Resources 10 would be like Musk, Bezos, Zuckerberg, Page, and Brin all deciding to trust each other enough to reduce their personal wealth to less then $1 million so they can form one mega-fund they all use together to... do what? Control the English speaking Internet more than they already do via X, Meta, and Alphabet as it is?<br /> <br /> It makes no sense. It can also be stopped by antitrust laws without blowing up the marketplace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, when discussing Resources, especially of this scale, it means there aren't singular things to target. </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're talking about Pooled Backgrounds, yes, there is, because there's an Anchor. Of course an Anchor Background isn't some specific physical object, but if your coterie has Domain as their Anchor, any Pooled Resources are tied to controlling that Domain. Losing access to that Domain means losing access to that wealth. The Domain is a nexus point in the scheme to control all that wealth as an undead monster that can't show up at board meetings, or meet with politicians during business hours, and so on, and control over the territory lets them get around such hurdles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think John Wicks basement stash in the first movie, but on a grander scale, and then he owns houses in every state or major country. </div> </div> </div>You're going on about what wealth is really like at these scales and using.. John Wick as an example? Seriously? Billionaires don't literally hide their money under the mattress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:49:32-07:00","id":1523930,"title":"","content":"No Billionaries hide their money in the sofa, but seriously there is so many legal ways to store there money and John Wick isn't meant to be taken seriously as it was a over the top action film with secret societies acting with such skill and influence that is unreal in it's scope of absurdity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-10-2023, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T06:44:41-07:00","id":1523950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523930#post1523930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Billionaries hide their money in the sofa, but seriously there is so many legal ways to store there money and John Wick isn't meant to be taken seriously as it was a over the top action film with secret societies acting with such skill and influence that is unreal in it's scope of absurdity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, you are mistaking the franchise concept for what the stash represents as far as the John Wick reference.<br /> <br /> For a hunter or other rival to attack your company infrastructure and banking to the degree that it would make a dent, they would need huge amounts of insider knowledge. So if they pull up the building permits on your haven, they will see the materials and notes required to figure that you installed a safe in the basement to hold your &quot;emergency fund&quot;, even if they don't know what is inside of it, they know something is there. Once they see that, they will look for other similar things at your other havens or properties. By building it yourself and covering it with concrete, there is no secret door to locate the stash and no records to indicate its existence. With high enough potence it wouldn't be that much more difficult to break open than drywall.<br /> <br /> As for what people with money actually do in the real world, I have lost track of the number of lawyers and business people I have met who keep &quot;emergency funds&quot; separate from banks to avoid transactional footprints and maintain liquidity. Sure, they are not going to keep a hundred million in cash in their mattress but keeping 50k to a couple million in an assortment of cash, jewelry, and small high value arts items is just good business sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T07:05:14-07:00","id":1523952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523922#post1523922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going on about what wealth is really like at these scales and using.. John Wick as an example? Seriously? Billionaires don't literally hide their money under the mattress.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how many millionaires and billionaires have you met and or done business with?<br /> <br /> To underline this fact, in California, having a net worth of two million means you own two or three houses and not much else. So, the notion of X amount of wealth or value automatically means a different way of doing things isn't correct. <br /> <br /> A smart business person doesn't keep all their eggs in one basket. Meaning only a portion of their wealth will be in liquid assets, a portion will be in investments, a portion will be things like property or businesses, and a portion will be relatively untraceable. The untraceable asset stash is usually something kept by the individuals who built their wealth on their own, thus learning to be extra careful or they had life experiences where they had to pull up stakes and run, such as what happens when countries go to war or ethnic cleansing starts occurring.<br /> <br /> A vampire can't stay in one place for too long lest they endanger the masquerade, so every decade or so they will move around. Couple this will the occasional need to fake their death, avoid a hunter, or get out of a city when the sabbat rolls through or one of the locals betrays them and you have a business person who is never going to be unprepared on some level for either starting over or at least ready for major setbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T12:34:37-07:00","id":1523959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523950#post1523950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, you are mistaking the franchise concept for what the stash represents as far as the John Wick reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stash represents John's hidden insecurities about being able to truly escape his old life even while starting a new one by burying a stash of supplies rather than getting rid of them.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the stash is nothing like what rich people IRL keep around if they need a large chunk of cash and for some reason don't want to leave a paper trail; or just want something liquid and easily transferred.<br /> <br /> The primary items of value in John's stash are all those coins. However, those coins are only good within a specific organization's system. They're not legal tender that can be used anywhere you want to go. This is,in fact, a plot point in the later movies because when John loses his privileges with the Continental, his coins become worthless as coins (in theory he could melt them down and sell the gold, but that's a lot less value than he gets out of them in the first film). <br /> <br /> The weapons are not things he keeps around as liquid assets. He uses them to kill people; making their financial resale value zero because they're evidence of crimes (and John is a famous assassin, so nobody that's going to buy a used gun on the down low is going to accept that the guns don't have a history).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By building it yourself and covering it with concrete, there is no secret door to locate the stash and no records to indicate its existence. With high enough potence it wouldn't be that much more difficult to break open than drywall. </div> </div> </div>1) If you're a vampire that's clearly got lots of cash on hand, they're going to assume you have stashes in your havens whether it's in the permits or not.<br /> <br /> 2) Hiding your stash in a fashion that requires destruction to access is highly impractical because it means you have to spend time (even with Potence handy) to dig it up when you need it. Auspex 1 is plenty to notice that something is off from the original construction and that there's a modification if a group of enemies is poking around your place to uncover your stashes. Or if they just burn down the building, you'll have to wait a considerable amount of time before you can dig up your hidden stashes without anyone watching the property seeing you do it. If you have to wait a month or two to get your stash, it doesn't do you any good if you need it by the end of the week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..to avoid transactional footprints... </div> </div> </div>I have doubts. Either you're passing off assumptions as facts,or you know a bunch of rich lawyers that freely admit to a crime to people that are willing to say that on the Internet.<br /> <br /> Purposefully avoiding such footprints is a crime, but one easily avoided/hard to prosecute because proving intent is really hard while being essential to proving the case. Pretty much the stupidest thing you can do if you want to avoid this paperwork is tell someone you're trying to evade the paperwork. Even if it's hearsay in court, it's probable cause for various regulatory and investigatory agencies to get warrants for your financial records and go over everything with a fine-toothed comb; pretty much undoing the whole &quot;keep this money/wealth on the down low&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523952#post1523952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how many millionaires and billionaires have you met and or done business with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To underline this fact, in California, having a net worth of two million means you own two or three houses and not much else. So, the notion of X amount of wealth or value automatically means a different way of doing things isn't correct. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what this has to do with anything I said. It undermines more of what you've been saying than anything else, since so much of what you're saying is about the subjective threshold where you can start using wealth in an entirely different context from people without less assets than you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..and a portion will be relatively untraceable. The untraceable asset stash is usually something kept by the individuals who built their wealth on their own, thus learning to be extra careful or they had life experiences where they had to pull up stakes and run, such as what happens when countries go to war or ethnic cleansing starts occurring. </div> </div> </div>Here-in lies the problem with what you're saying.<br /> <br /> Most ultra-rich people have a decent amount of untraceable wealth just because they buy rich person shit. They don't need a stash of gold to avoid taxes. Most financial transactions aren't public records to worry about that. They're not worried about a bank form on file with the IRS that they took out $100K and it's just sitting in a safe or three in case they want some spending cash and don't want to have to deal with the PitA of getting that kind of money from the bank. They have that sort of thing as a mixture of convenience and showing off.<br /> <br /> I know three men who spent almost half a million dollars combined, in cash (and they didn't need to use cash, their credit cards don't have limits, they were showing off) buying cases of the most expense alcohol they could find around town because they were in a dick-waving contest to see who could impress a mutual business partner at the fourth person's child's wedding. They love having significant cash on hand because they love being able to buy immediately things most people could never afford. The idea that rich people are hoarding secret stashes of untraceable assets for nefarious purposes is something that's either biased from who you know, or your own spin on things.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;bug out&quot; stash? Sure that happens.but the vast majority of ultra-rich people both (a) live in places of minimal risk in that regard and (b) already have options in other countries. There's good reason nobody is buying Bob Mendez's claim that he has a gigantic stockpile of cash and gold (and a car) because he internalized keeping a bug-out stash from his family's history of fleeing troubled parts of the world.<br /> <br /> I know two people that are venture capitalists that specialize in developing African countries. It's risky work because it means going to places that have recent histories of extreme political corruption, sectarian and/or genocidal violence, and so on, as they try to be the first major investors on the ground when it looks like things are finally stabilizing. They have had to bribe their way out of countries because they jumped in too early. They've had to do a lot of &quot;creative&quot; financing because a lot of people they have to do business with to do business like they do have international sanctions. They do a lot of the things you are talking about, but for exceedingly different reasons that you ascribe to the kind of people that do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire can't stay in one place for too long lest they endanger the masquerade, so every decade or so they will move around. </div> </div> </div>This isn't the premise of the game. At all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T14:28:55-07:00","id":1523966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523959#post1523959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have doubts. Either you're passing off assumptions as facts,or you know a bunch of rich lawyers that freely admit to a crime to people that are willing to say that on the Internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why you don't know what you are talking about, it isn't a crime to have your money in your possession. There is a fundamental difference between making money and not paying taxes on it verses making money with taxes paid and then relocating it to an undisclosed location or converting it to a different form of asset. If the funds are paid out or withdrawn in an appropriate manner, it isn't illegal. But once it has left the bank or the business, there is no paper trail, which means what it is traded for can't be tracked. <br /> <br /> Buying scrap silver or gold for cash and then melting it down into small ingots means there are no serial numbers and no item description to track. Not all jewels have micro serial numbers etched into them. Likewise it is entirely possible to pay for goods and services by trading expensive items such as antiques, art, or other collectables. This is not illegal to do and is often done to blur the value of a transaction in a legal fashion.<br /> <br /> Now the knee jerk reaction to this is to assume a bulk withdrawal that sets off loads of flags in various banking systems. But if you have dozens or hundreds of smaller transactions then the system don't trigger. Also since we a dealing with vampires here, they have the time to move small amounts of wealth around and accumulate it into sizable off grid stashes, think hoarders but with unlimited lifespans and they only collect treasure rather than junk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T15:24:12-07:00","id":1523970,"title":"","content":"I think part of the answer to this question depends on a group/ST\u2019s gaming philosophy.<br /> <br /> For instance on one hand, if I\u2019m running a chronicle using a more character-path method of storytelling, I may look at the sheets of all the player characters and think to myself \u201cOkay John\u2019s Ventrue has Finance 5 &amp; Resources 5, he probably wants some challenges that can be solved with money and some type of financial challenges and storylines. Maybe I\u2019ll design a vampiric rival who\u2019s seeking to undercut his PC\u2019s investments as part of the larger schemes of the campaign\u201d. In a situation like that you could say that the ST is forcing conflict but in some ways that\u2019s the Storytellers job (like how a writer\u2019s job for a movie is to create conflict in the story). Now I agree that it can be done poorly and feel forced but if played naturally and written well it\u2019s just classic storytelling techniques.<br /> <br /> On the other hand maybe I\u2019m running a more sandbox/open-world style chronicle. In that case the scenarios may become more realistic although perhaps having a double edged sword depending on perspective. If I\u2019m setting up a sandbox campaign then I probably want to seed it with a wide variety of potential events, challenges, and threats that could occur in play; some of which might be very easy to solve just by dumping money into them. But that\u2019s part of what makes a sandbox shine, sometimes you\u2019ll be able to solve problems immediately and sometimes you really won\u2019t. So if you\u2019re running a money build certain challenges (all the money in the world won\u2019t stop the mayor\u2019s daughter from being a mage who wants to buy your ancestral estate) might not have immediate answers. That\u2019s how the play style goes and it\u2019s up to the ST to try and keep things interesting by keeping in mind the consequences of what the various story actors are doing and what effects they might have.<br /> <br /> Also, if I\u2019m running a chronicle and someone has basically made a character with a perfected hermit-crab build who never needs to leave a controlled environment and interact with the chronicle in a meaningful way, I may just talk to that player and ask them to make that PC a secondary character that we can blue-book over longer time spans but that they should make a new primary character who can be more involved in the mean level of play that the group is engaged in. <br /> <br /> Those are some of my thoughts on the resource question, I hope that they can be of some use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T19:12:52-07:00","id":1523983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523966#post1523966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why you don't know what you are talking about, it isn't a crime to have your money in your possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... if you want to sound authoritative on this matter, you shouldn't be making absolute statements like this. If it is never a crime to have your money in your possession, nobody would launder money. There are a large number of situations that can result in your money needing to stay where it is until that situation is resolved. There are financial vehicles where not touching your money until a duration expires is part of the deal (though breaking that isn't generally a crime, getting sued or getting hit with a large penalty isn't great to have to deal with).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a fundamental difference between making money and not paying taxes on it verses making money with taxes paid and then relocating it to an undisclosed location or converting it to a different form of asset. </div> </div> </div>When did I talk about tax fraud?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the knee jerk reaction to this is to assume a bulk withdrawal that sets off loads of flags in various banking systems. But if you have dozens or hundreds of smaller transactions then the system don't trigger. </div> </div> </div>Now you're showing you have never dealt with the BSA before.<br /> <br /> Bulk withdraws don't actually set off loads of flags. Big transactions happen all the time. It's 1 to 2 pages of paperwork to tack on to it for the BSA filing you bank has to do.<br /> <br /> Structuring is an actual crime. Purposefully making a large number of small transactions in order to go under the standard reporting thresholds is the definition of structuring. As I noted, structuring is an extremely hard crime to prove (most BSA violations aren't charged because they're people that do things like tell their bank that they want to withdraw $9999.99 because there's a form if they did a full $10K... only to then have to talk to a BSA compliance bank employee and fill out a lot of paperwork to avoid the bank reporting it as a criminal act), but that's why you don't tell anyone that you're doing it.<br /> <br /> Put please, person that doesn't seem to know that structuring is a crime, tell me more about my ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T10:16:41-07:00","id":1524006,"title":"","content":"On the matter of John Wick. Deep down he knew that he couldn't escape the actions of his past life no matter how much he wished it and his late wife bringing out buried elements of his personality that could've gotten himself killed in his line of work and his stash was all practical stuff like his weapons and the gold coins that he needs to use to access perks of his former life and it didn't serve him well as he got kicked out of the club and was at a huge disadvantage as they knew what type of aliases he might use or contacts he might go to in times of help.<br /> <br /> If I was going to use a movie for a source of help in such matters, I'd probably use the Jason Bourne series by Matt Damon over the John Wick material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T11:53:01-07:00","id":1524046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1523983#post1523983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bulk withdraws don't actually set off loads of flags. Big transactions happen all the time. It's 1 to 2 pages of paperwork to tack on to it for the BSA filing you bank has to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>By your own admission any transfer of $10,000 is automatically flagged, whereas anything below that isn't automatically flagged. You are not proving your point, if anything you are proving mine.<br /> <br /> Structuring is a charge that was created not to be a crime by itself, but to add on top of other crimes to create weight to the charges. Otherwise, every senior citizen that withdraws a couple hundred a month could be charged with structuring. Once again, this only comes into play when someone is already certain of your guilt and is looking for additional stuff to throw at you.<br /> <br /> When it comes to records and financial institutions you have to pick one of two routes, the first is invisibility and the second is immunity. If you pick immunity, you do everything on the up and up, which means even if someone gets cranky and tries to maliciously audit you, there is nothing to attack. Alternatively with invisibility option you are going to do criminal things, but everything is setup to avoid attention and misdirect any investigation. <br /> <br /> Since we are discussing vampires here, of course there is a level of criminality that will always go on, so the key is to avoid attention and any extra paperwork. Which in turn means you make sure all taxes on traceable funds are paid in full so no one can leverage the financials, you always keep payments in small amounts spread across multiple businesses so no one can easily see how the money moves, and you routinely convert traceable funds into untraceable goods which are stored in multiple locations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T12:21:05-07:00","id":1524050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1524046#post1524046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By your own admission any transfer of $10,000 is automatically flagged, whereas anything below that isn't automatically flagged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reported and flagged aren't the same thing. Every tax return is a report of your finances to the government, it doesn't mean your return is flagged. It's just on file. $10K+ transfers are flagged by banks... to file BSA reports for their compliance officer(s), not flagged by the government for investigation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are not proving your point, if anything you are proving mine. </div> </div> </div>Not really. You talked about real world lawyers admitting to you that they were structuring to you. Your counter-point was basically that structuring wasn't a crime, but once called on out on that you've simply moved the goal posts; fundamentally admitting your original point was wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Structuring is a charge that was created not to be a crime by itself, but to add on top of other crimes to create weight to the charges. </div> </div> </div>Why it was made a crime doesn't change that it is a crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise, every senior citizen that withdraws a couple hundred a month could be charged with structuring. Once again, this only comes into play when someone is already certain of your guilt and is looking for additional stuff to throw at you. </div> </div> </div>So, you're reinforcing everything I've been saying about how little structuring is actually charged because proving the intent is so hard and lots of people do structuring-like activity without even knowing that it's a thing? Thanks for agreeing with me on that at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to records and financial institutions you have to pick one of two routes, the first is invisibility and the second is immunity. </div> </div> </div>Immunity isn't really that hard if your someone in the Resources 4-5 area anyway. The reason to pick immunity is because those reports are full of non-binding &quot;intention&quot; statements. You're already doing thing like diversely investing in a wide portfolio. Transfer $500K (liquidate some stocks for a paper lose while you're at it, since your stocks portfolio isn't a banking account, hence you need to transfer it to spend it), put on the form that it's for a real estate bid, put in a low ball bid, lose to someone else. You now have $500K in a different account to spend on whatever you want that can easily avoid scrutiny as you're dealing with smaller expenses or large expenditures that mesh with your existing portfolio. As long as there's nobody to testify that your intent was fraud (because <u>you don't tell people what you're doing </u>), you're still safely immune despite a bit of fraud because it's fraud that's impossible to prove unless you confessed it. There's no reason for this to change for vampires.<br /> <br /> You're not wrong about what happens once you have the funds in a place where you can spread them out with less attention. It's the intermediary parts you're wrong about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T10:24:55-07:00","id":1524063,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you are fundamentally missing the fact that all vampires don't have rights and that the laws don't recognize them. So regardless of what they pick or do, they are committing a crime by your definition. Faking your death is illegal, creating fake identities is illegal, operating a 100% legal business with false ownership papers is illegal. I get that you are wanting to pedantically argue about IRL financial advice and legality as if this was a financial forum. But it's a game forum about undead doing horrible and illegal things as a matter of course before breakfast. <br /> <br /> So could you please decide whether we are arguing about IRL financial strategy or in-game fluff that helps add another level of play to characters who want to run business characters and use the Resources Background in new and interesting ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T02:19:39-07:00","id":1524088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1524063#post1524063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you are fundamentally missing the fact that all vampires don't have rights and that the laws don't recognize them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. If vampires want Resources at a high level, they need do understand things like what is and isn't legal, and what level of attention various illegalities are likely to result in. They're engaging with a human society that defaults to thinking of them as still being human; and thus reacts as if a human did the things a vampire does.<br /> <br /> In finance, esp. where there's a whole net in place to try and catch suspicious activity that's nothing like dealing with violent crime, understanding that net is vital for a vampire that wants to maintain high amounts of wealth without exposing that they're a vampire and all the consequence therein.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So regardless of what they pick or do, they are committing a crime by your definition. </div> </div> </div>My definition? Would you like me to cite the relevant statues or something?<br /> <br /> My point, was that you were citing IRL lawyers that told you there were structuring, to which I expressed doubt, because lawyers aren't generally in the habit of admitting to crimes unless they're in deep trouble; or maybe they aren't the financial experts you're trying to leech the presumed authority of.to support your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Faking your death is illegal, </div> </div> </div>Actually it isn't. It can be something someone does in furtherance of other crimes, but there's no law against faking your death. Many vampires are going to fake their death are part of illegal activity because they aren't going to walk away from all of their stuff that they'd have to leave behind if they wanted to fake their death in a legal fashion. Most vampires don't want to turn themselves into a non-person in the eyes of the law compared to breaking the law and using faking their death as part of the plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So could you please decide whether we are arguing about IRL financial strategy or in-game fluff that helps add another level of play to characters who want to run business characters and use the Resources Background in new and interesting ways? </div> </div> </div>Oh shove it.<br /> <br /> The RL financial stuff and John Wick is the only stuff you responded to. If you want to focus the conversation on Vampire the game, and vampires within it, there's plenty of things I've posted in the thread you've completely ignored to have nitpicky legal/financial debates. Spare me the obnoxious &quot;victim card&quot; routine. The direction of this conversation has largely been steered by your choices in what to respond to; part of your whole point earlier in the thread was that part of the problem with Resources is that the game (and most people playing it) have no idea how al of this works IRL to make adjudicating how to manage the trait in the game highly fraught (an assessment I agree with if that wasn't clear). If you want to focus on vampires, I'll happily do so.<br /> <br /> But if you're going to come at me with ad hominem crap, don't bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T05:19:05-07:00","id":1524094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1524088#post1524088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh shove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that sums up the quality of your position rather well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T10:47:22-07:00","id":1524107,"title":"","content":"In an effort to get back to the original post. Mr. Hello was asking if having high resources makes conflicts feel forced and the majority of the answers were that having money doesn\u2019t end problems and in fact causes a whole slew of new troubles for you and others as many people don\u2019t know how money is truly made. The same could be said about how some gamers think how security teams work and use them as front line soldiers instead how they really work in the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-15-2023, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T23:31:08-07:00","id":1524127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523460-anyone-else-feel-that-at-a-certain-resource-level-vtm-becomes-forced?p=1524107#post1524107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">many people don\u2019t know...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I don't know witch is &quot;worse&quot; to encounter in a Game be a player or a storyteller, a player/players who don't know how things work.. or the ones who <i>know </i>?<br /> Alchemy, Path of Conjuring, Biothaumaturgy, Daimonion's Psychomachia\u200b just to name a few is <i>deadly </i>in the hands of those who done their homework and <i>know </i>how things works<br /> Same with the merits or flaws<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T01:07:12-07:00","id":1524128,"title":"","content":"There is a significant difference with Resources, in that it's a common Background, with even an implied idea that having it means your character has some idea of how to make use of it in broad strokes (ex; V20 says to call for Wits + Resources as a potential roll for managing your character's finances). Rare Discipline and Thaumaturgy Paths are pretty easy to tell if a player might get disruptive with them by trying to leverage that sort of &quot;homework.&quot; Coming up with reasons to have them in the first place, and likely Knowledges like Science to explain how their characters would know specific applications are pretty big flags a player intends to use some of the powers that can be extremely potent with some creativity.<br /> <br /> IME it's far easier to deal with people that don't know specific in-depth topics in play, because we naturally abstract most of that anyway. A big part of all these mechanics in the first place is so that characters can perform actions that the players can't. It's great if a player does some research if they make a character that was an avid rock climber before being Embraced so they can naturally role-play various things. But it's easy enough to hand wave, &quot;Can I use Athletics instead of Survival for some rope work since my character should know how to tie ropes climbers use?&quot; and not worry about the specific knot names and which is best for what<br /> <br /> Most players that do know topics in depth do also know not to go overboard with it because it's a game where we're all trying to have fun. But it's a lot harder to deal with players who are correct about various obscure topic, make characters that have every reason to know those things, and then use that to try to &quot;get one over&quot; on the ST or even other players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T12:22:22-07:00","id":1524204,"title":"","content":"They can be both trying Shadowprowler from other games, but so far my WOD gaming group have been quite positive and it helps that we stick to what we really know and not try get ourselves into scenes that we are not very knowledgeable about. We don't how the world works for people like Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos, Bill Gates, Donald Trump, or Vince McMahon of W,W.E. who are worth billions of dollars and I don't think the resources rating for VTM doesn't really cover things at that level and is more local or regional at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-17-2023, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T04:56:30-07:00","id":1524222,"title":"","content":"Well, there is this little thing that you must make a compelling history to be multibillionaire, but once there os the story, just roll with it. Billionaires are very good in not having many obvious ties with their fortunes, like fiscal paradises, houses in the name of trust funds and many, many other ways to evade taxes. And unless you do something outrageous, like building a dome over your city, or avoiding the sun to shining over a whole place, most certainly you can just go whit that without bigger problems with that. Even in the case of a bankruptcy in one or more of your enterprises, you still can just throw your money around the globe. And we're talking about a species that is evading taxes since the Egyptian Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T16:34:38-07:00","id":1524248,"title":"","content":"Your right MrDrika and I can't think of a good way why say my Malkavian would be at level of wealth to begin with and it doesn't quite fit the notion in mind for my player character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T19:16:34-07:00","id":1524251,"title":"","content":"What kind of Malk you have in mind? I guess depressive or some level of sociopathy would work better, but with a bit of creativity, you can explore the whole spectrum. Dementation... is a must have, Eyes of Chaos can be adapted wonderfully both to stock market and to real estate speculation, and without this petty cares of compassion or empathy, is no problem to hire a lawyer firm to a project of gentrification of some neighborhood or another. And about why you need all that money? Mostly protection but also because blood is such high stakes these days, and there are some days you just can't &quot;live&quot;, and you need to hire some three or four hookers because the Beast will howl until you give their share. Also, (and here some paranoia may sweep) they want your hide, and escaping is easier if you can escape discreetly via some gentlemen that know how to be silent, or maybe won't remember you in their broken minds. There are many ways to keep a filthy rich Malk. Even to protect their fortune by ways of a accounting organization that would make Babel's library look like a Very hungry caterpillar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T09:25:17-07:00","id":1524280,"title":"","content":"I see him more as a seeker of lore like Hesha and uses his natural charisma to get people including the most haughty of Ventrue or Lasombra to relax and tell him stuff that they know for sure and if he can find the stuff they are looking for he will help for future boons. He came from a well off family and would've sold some items that would be considered expensive, but would keep the truly priceless or sentitmental stuff that meant a great deal to him. Since he likes to learn things I'd went with a 